cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment: Lean formalization"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/einstein-relation-lean"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Quantitative Einstein relation for
  reversible diffusions in a random environment" by Ahmed Bou-Rabee and Ruizhe Xu. Every
  numbered result of the paper except Conjecture 1.3 is stated and proved, including the
  main theorem (Theorem 1.2: the velocity divided by the force differs from the
  diffusivity in the force direction by at most a constant times the force) and its
  sharpness (Proposition 7.1). The proofs are conditional on thirty results from the
  literature, which are explicit Prop-valued hypotheses of the theorems, not axioms. The
  library contains no sorry and no custom axiom, and Theorem 1.2 and Proposition 7.1 each
  have a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Ruizhe
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - Einstein relation
  - random environment
  - stochastic homogenization
license: Apache-2.0
references:
